WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.497
This example brings several object-oriented ideas
together

00:00:03.524 --> 00:00:06.645
in a small analytics class The class

00:00:06.658 --> 00:00:09.868
is named SalesReport Its purpose is to

00:00:09.895 --> 00:00:11.895
store a collection of sales values and

00:00:11.921 --> 00:00:16.079
provide several related summary calculations The
dunder

00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:18.013
init method receives a list of sales

00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:19.816
and stores it in self dot sales

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.868
The first method is total sales It

00:00:23.895 --> 00:00:25.816
returns the sum of all values in

00:00:25.842 --> 00:00:28.776
the list The second method is average

00:00:28.803 --> 00:00:31.895
sale It adds all sales values and

00:00:31.921 --> 00:00:34.882
divides by the number of values The

00:00:34.908 --> 00:00:37.961
third method is high sales count This

00:00:37.974 --> 00:00:41.158
method receives a cutoff value It starts

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:42.961
a counter at zero loops through each

00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:45.316
sale and increases the counter whenever a

00:00:45.342 --> 00:00:46.921
sale is greater than or equal to

00:00:46.947 --> 00:00:50.592
the cutoff Finally it returns the count

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.289
Next we create one SalesReport object using

00:00:54.316 --> 00:00:56.513
the values one hundred twenty two hundred

00:00:56.539 --> 00:00:59.605
fifty one hundred seventy-five three hundred twenty

00:00:59.776 --> 00:01:02.658
and ninety Before you run the cell

00:01:02.908 --> 00:01:05.776
let us predict the output The total

00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:07.711
of these five values is nine hundred

00:01:07.737 --> 00:01:11.658
fifty-five The average is one hundred ninety-one

00:01:12.592 --> 00:01:14.447
If the cutoff is two hundred only

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.553
two values meet or exceed the cutoff

00:01:16.803 --> 00:01:18.934
two hundred fifty and three hundred twenty

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.816
Click Run now The terminal should show

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:25.263
total sales of nine hundred fifty-five an

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:27.355
average sale of one hundred ninety-one point

00:01:27.368 --> 00:01:29.197
zero and two sales at least two

00:01:29.224 --> 00:01:31.960
hundred Now change the cutoff in the

00:01:31.987 --> 00:01:33.776
final line from two hundred to one

00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:38.105
hundred fifty Run the cell again More

00:01:38.132 --> 00:01:41.211
values should now meet the threshold This

00:01:41.237 --> 00:01:43.026
example shows when a class can be

00:01:43.053 --> 00:01:46.434
useful in analytics The data and several

00:01:46.461 --> 00:01:50.697
repeated actions belong together The SalesReport
object

00:01:50.711 --> 00:01:53.039
stores the sales values and provides methods

00:01:53.066 --> 00:01:54.645
that summarize those values
